        "original_id": "b7b79e6a-1528-508a-8be4-fc3cc89975cb",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: Vilayat Khan, Ravi Shankar, Ali Akbar Khan, Nikhil Banerjee, Imrat Khan, Baba Allauddin Khan, Enayat Khan, Sheema Mukherjee\n- Topics: Indian classical music, sitar, introducing Indian classical music to the West\n\nFacts:\n- Vilayat Khan, Ravi Shankar, Ali Akbar Khan, Nikhil Banerjee, and Imrat Khan helped introduce Indian classical music to the West.\n- Nikhil Banerjee was a student of Baba Allauddin Khan.\n- Nikhil Banerjee was known for technical virtuosity and clinical execution.\n- Enayat Khan was the father of Vilayat Khan.\n- Vilayat Khan was regarded as one of the top sitar players of the postwar period.\n- Sheema Mukherjee is the niece of Nikhil Banerjee.",
        "type": "TextSummary"
      },
